 ## Overview
-CD-TVD is the first diffusion-based approach for scientific volume super-resolution, designed to upscale low-resolution volumetric data to higher resolutions [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from prior GAN-based methods by combining contrastive pre-training on historical simulation data with fine-tuning from as few as one high-resolution timestep, achieving higher fidelity (43–48 dB PSNR) on fluid dynamics datasets [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard image SR methods that rely on VGG-based perceptual losses, CD-TVD employs a contrastive encoding module to learn degradation-aware features in latent space, providing domain-specific representations better suited for scientific data [S1, unofficial].
+CD-TVD is the first diffusion-based approach for scientific volume super-resolution, designed to upscale low-resolution volumetric data to higher resolutions [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from prior GAN-based methods by combining contrastive pre-training on historical simulation data with fine-tuning from as few as one high-resolution timestep, achieving 43–48 dB PSNR on four fluid dynamics datasets at 4× upscaling [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard image SR methods that rely on VGG-based perceptual losses, CD-TVD employs a contrastive encoding module to learn degradation-aware features in latent space, providing domain-specific representations better suited for scientific data [S1, unofficial].
 
